        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF149 adds support for <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLElement.captureStream()</code> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2017708\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2017708</a> - and this was recoreded in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3995050060\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29135\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29135/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29135\">#29135</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Previously only a non-standards-compliant version <code class=\"notranslate\">mozCaptureSttream()</code> was defined. The docs contained notes about the compliance issues. This attempts to move those to BCD, where they belong.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related work for this can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3978086146\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43215\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43215/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43215\">mdn/content#43215</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29165",
            "title": "HTMLMediaElement.captureStream - add notes",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-03T06:41:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-03T06:40:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68780890?u=ead4e493844141826b3007c4bbf730edd1df630a&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updates <code class=\"notranslate\">api.AudioParam.cancelScheduledValues</code> to mark partial support for older Chrome/Safari versions and Firefox.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Per the March 2020 spec update (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"501625877\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/WebAudio/web-audio-api/issues/2071\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/WebAudio/web-audio-api/issues/2071/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/WebAudio/web-audio-api/issues/2071\">WebAudio/web-audio-api#2071</a>), <code class=\"notranslate\">cancelScheduledValues</code> should cancel in-progress curve events created by <code class=\"notranslate\">setValueCurveAtTime</code>. Chrome and Safari have implemented this behavior, but Firefox has not.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Supported by the following implementation evidence and release notes:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Chrome</strong>:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Chromium bug: <a href=\"https://crbug.com/1063502\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1063502</a></li>\n<li>Implementation: <a href=\"https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/7a87148abe74349f55729acfbd54ebb02418aac6\" rel=\"nofollow\">Commit 7a87148a</a></li>\n<li>Release: <a href=\"https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commits?commit=7a87148abe74349f55729acfbd54ebb02418aac6&amp;platform=Windows\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chrome 83</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Safari</strong>:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>WebKit bug: <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=216132\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 216132</a></li>\n<li>Implementation: <a href=\"https://trac.webkit.org/changeset/266558\" rel=\"nofollow\">Changeset r266558</a></li>\n<li>Release: <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/11300/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-114/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Safari TP 114</a>, <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/11648/new-webkit-features-in-safari-14-1/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Safari 14.1</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Firefox</strong>:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Not implemented (<a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1752775\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1752775</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29029.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3931073911\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29029\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29029/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29029\">#29029</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29150",
